<%# Reset the corner widget's own composer. The message itself arrives through
    Message#broadcasts_to, which appends to every .conversation-log on the page.
    On validation failure we re-render the same form with the invalid message.

    A fresh Message on success, and only the rejected one on failure. Passing
    @message unconditionally reset nothing: form_with on a persisted record emits
    method="patch" and refills the textarea with the text that was just sent, so
    the composer kept the message visible and turned into an edit form for it.
    routes.rb declares `resources :messages, only: [ :create ]`, so there is no
    PATCH route and the second send could not succeed. %>
<%= turbo_stream.replace "nearby_widget_message" do %>
  <%= render "nearby/widget_composer",
        conversation: @conversation,
        message: @message.persisted? ? Message.new : @message %>
<% end %>
